      "title": "Ruby2ßhell: Pre-authentication RCE on stock Rails",
      "url": "https://verialabs.com/ruby2shell/",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50556287",
      "score": 380,
      "comments": 160,
      "author": "jdns",
      "published": "2026-11-19T05:09:11Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Pre-authentication flaw exposes default Ruby on Rails deployments to zero-interaction remote code execution without requiring custom application-level vulnerabilities.",
        "Attack vector exploits Ruby Unicode case-mapping quirks (notably the sharp S 'ß') during framework-level request parsing and processing.",
        "Security teams should immediately audit internet-exposed Rails instances, inspect WAF telemetry for Unicode anomalies, and apply incoming vendor patches."
      ]
    },
